                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cb5eacb-99d9-3004-bbce-67018a731f19",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A supply of resources."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fb96fbb-e5c5-4889-b283-b16f4bb4130e",
                                                "sense_id": "3cb5eacb-99d9-3004-bbce-67018a731f19",
                                                "text": "The 4-BEP and 4-CEP stock is maintained in a common pool for both Chatham and South Eastern fast main-line services."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b36388c6-b634-310f-9211-454db55138e6",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A supply of resources.",
                                            "A number of people when considered as a resource."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27fa8cba-d5e1-42ee-a6cb-37f64a0586cb",
                                                "sense_id": "b36388c6-b634-310f-9211-454db55138e6",
                                                "text": "dating pool"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1904893-9459-49e1-a294-56474f40e3d1",
                                                "sense_id": "b36388c6-b634-310f-9211-454db55138e6",
                                                "text": "There is a limited pool of candidates from which to choose the new manager."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a228b50e-b1d4-43a9-bcdf-dfcc4f849f2b",
                                                "sense_id": "b36388c6-b634-310f-9211-454db55138e6",
                                                "text": "This is not necessarily surprising; employers often use recessions to pay new workers less because they have such a large pool of potential applicants to choose from, says Ruth Milkman, the Labor Studies Chair at the City University of New York’s School of Labor and Urban Studies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb55e73a-8277-3796-98e3-6fba2c1af3a4",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A game at billiards, in which each of the players stakes a certain sum, the winner taking the whole; also, in public billiard rooms, a game in which the loser pays the entrance fee for all who engage in the game."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c965e954-34a7-3dcd-b518-51f3bed91389",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cue sport played on a pool table. There are 15 balls, 7 of one colour or solids, 7 of another color or stripes, and the black ball (also called the 8 ball). A player must pocket all their own colour balls and then the black ball in order to win."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a352e8ca-9b57-4af2-8d2d-3d5274bff680",
                                                "sense_id": "c965e954-34a7-3dcd-b518-51f3bed91389",
                                                "text": "He plays pool at the billiard-houses, and may be seen engaged at cards and dominoes of forenoons."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb7bf3d2-d329-3e43-8249-4351d22a7aa4",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In rifle shooting, a contest in which each competitor pays a certain sum for every shot he makes, the net proceeds being divided among the winners."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0905158e-be5c-36b0-87af-8591e917fa32",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of fencers taking part in a competition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "799c6bbc-5048-310b-8d1d-8be2e4341d3c",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A set of teams playing each other in the same division, while not during the same period playing any teams that belong to other sets in the division."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "458103db-8bcb-3e2b-b56b-8a26cf52b9b8",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any gambling or commercial venture in which several persons join."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01514eac-771d-3f8b-9078-3ed1f0836c25",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stake played for in certain games of cards, billiards, etc.; an aggregated stake to which each player has contributed a share; also, the receptacle for the stakes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a90a99b2-2ee0-3dd7-aa39-81bb55e4b728",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A combination of persons contributing money to be used for the purpose of increasing or depressing the market price of stocks, grain, or other commodities; also, the aggregate of the sums so contributed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1784c98-f525-4b78-963c-779c8b7ab301",
                                                "sense_id": "a90a99b2-2ee0-3dd7-aa39-81bb55e4b728",
                                                "text": "The pool took all the wheat offered below the limit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "386b649f-e842-42a3-a736-a5d4a6cedadd",
                                                "sense_id": "a90a99b2-2ee0-3dd7-aa39-81bb55e4b728",
                                                "text": "He put $10,000 into the pool."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c35c8b80-8b34-3be1-8d1e-b5f24a085e5e",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A set of players in quadrille etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2caee8a2-70d2-31b2-ba3e-ef3905e0f635",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mutual arrangement between competing lines, by which the receipts of all are aggregated, and then distributed pro rata according to agreement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3aaea0c6-9755-328b-8f2c-b1c33e81ff3e",
                                        "entry_id": "05551b50-3f67-3964-8584-9fe3c5f693dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An aggregation of properties or rights, belonging to different people in a community, in a common fund, to be charged with common liabilities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pool",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4467457e-e450-3a58-ab6a-be59dfc482b7",
                                        "entry_id": "2a9bbefd-bed9-3b3f-8548-cd5fbcff3f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put together; contribute to a common fund, on the basis of a mutual division of profits or losses; to make a common interest of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92d364b6-9d14-4f06-8ba5-974a9b0ebdba",
                                                "sense_id": "4467457e-e450-3a58-ab6a-be59dfc482b7",
                                                "text": "We must pool our resources."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71cc60d1-2bf3-4ee0-8d52-1538c49b2055",
                                                "sense_id": "4467457e-e450-3a58-ab6a-be59dfc482b7",
                                                "text": "“She must be exceedingly clever to have beaten the police the way she has for the last few years; and—er—I worship at the shrine of cleverness—especially if it be a woman’s. The idea struck me last night that if she and I should—er—pool our resources, we should not have to complain of the reward.”\n“Oh, so youse wants to work wid her, eh?” sniffed Rhoda Gray. “So dat’s it, is it?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33360dab-1baa-40cd-99d7-64fe2868ab23",
                                                "sense_id": "4467457e-e450-3a58-ab6a-be59dfc482b7",
                                                "text": "It all started 6 years ago, as Rutgers University scientists Allan Conney, Ph.D., and George C. Wagner, Ph.D., chatted at an office get-together. […] From this conversation, the two decided to pool their knowledge and join forces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13010e37-b7fa-4f4a-86b7-67f46732fe3b",
                                                "sense_id": "4467457e-e450-3a58-ab6a-be59dfc482b7",
                                                "text": "27 February 2010, Barack Obama, Presidential Weekly Address - Time for Us to Act\nMany on both sides agreed that we should give small businesses and individuals the ability to participate in a new insurance marketplace – which members of Congress would also use – that would allow them to pool their purchasing power and get a better deal from insurance companies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9f9f8d7-94eb-371e-b497-4f35b79f22a0",
                                        "entry_id": "2a9bbefd-bed9-3b3f-8548-cd5fbcff3f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To combine or contribute with others, as for a commercial, speculative, or gambling transaction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ad5c010e-f87c-417e-93b6-8983eca29da0",
                        "source_entry_id": "158b82b7-aa7f-3402-a174-3acb4b31fb0d",
                        "source_sense_id": "996aceba-62d1-394a-a17f-41d15f9df572",
                        "target_lang_word": "swimming-bath",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dfa5b249-3c5d-4fff-90ae-36b54c0e1b6d",
                        "source_entry_id": "158b82b7-aa7f-3402-a174-3acb4b31fb0d",
                        "source_sense_id": "996aceba-62d1-394a-a17f-41d15f9df572",
                        "target_lang_word": "swimming-pool",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "swimming-pool",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5389dc21-8647-34e2-955d-94ca81e2bc5d",
                                        "entry_id": "6e8a4ea4-1520-3619-a8e7-be7a8163588e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dated form of swimming pool."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b113c141-3429-44b0-adfd-45c7dddb2ef0",
                                                "sense_id": "5389dc21-8647-34e2-955d-94ca81e2bc5d",
                                                "text": "Inevitably, the Comptess went so far as to offer her (and hence us, when we were there) the use of their bijou swimming-pool, which her sons had cleared of algae and water-beetles just before her arrival."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89f2b76e-9d23-4532-8370-4909c18540fb",
                                                "sense_id": "5389dc21-8647-34e2-955d-94ca81e2bc5d",
                                                "text": "I love especially to think of the Lady Margaret’s ancient foundation of Christ’s College with the bowling-green, the deep swimming-pool, and Milton’s mulberry tree."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e7f8fb4-582b-4e46-97db-16a85b0f0f7e",
                                                "sense_id": "5389dc21-8647-34e2-955d-94ca81e2bc5d",
                                                "text": "Swimming-pools for ladies, children and gentlemen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9e4effd-d683-474d-81dc-dcaf156ccca2",
                                                "sense_id": "5389dc21-8647-34e2-955d-94ca81e2bc5d",
                                                "text": "If half a dozen swimming-pools on either river were inclosed with canvas screens, and strictly reserved for the use of men, the most earnest moralist, even if provided with a powerful field-glass, would strive in vain to undermine his moral nature from the deck of a passing steam-boat, and the men of the poorer classes could secure a daily bath in comparative comfort."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecb355d6-9fd1-4628-963f-ac204596ec2c",
                                                "sense_id": "5389dc21-8647-34e2-955d-94ca81e2bc5d",
                                                "text": "Nakedness is wholly inappropriate in almost all social situations and, even in situations where much naked flesh is exposed (on the beach, at the swimming-pool, even in the bedroom), the bodies that meet there are likely to be adorned, if only by jewellery, or indeed, even perfume: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fce9dd2-46e4-46ec-b3ff-8f64cb091a0f",
                                                "sense_id": "5389dc21-8647-34e2-955d-94ca81e2bc5d",
                                                "text": "There is a sudden cut—they are left in darkness for a few seconds—and then a small swimming-pool comes into view, with four or five people in it (“That’s my uncle and aunt’s pool,” Evian says, “We used to go there a lot, in the summer. I used to get on really well with my cousin Nadine, we’re the same age.”)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "982144dc-2abf-4e0c-b6e5-ada340ef4804",
                        "source_entry_id": "158b82b7-aa7f-3402-a174-3acb4b31fb0d",
